claim.claim-text:
receive one or more frames for a workload;
determine one or more compute resource parameters of the plurality of streaming microprocessors for the workload;
use the compute resource parameters to schedule compute resources to process the additional one or more frames for the workload; and
update the compute resource parameters in the local cache memory.

receive an additional one or more frames for the workload;
retrieve the one or more compute resource parameters from the local cache memory; and use the compute resource parameters to schedule compute resources to process the
additional one or more frames for the workload.

receiving, in a general purpose graphics processor comprising a plurality of streaming multiprocessors (SMs) comprising a plurality of processing resources and a local cache memory, one or more frames for a workload;
determining one or more compute resource parameters of the plurality of streaming microprocessors for the workload;
using the compute resource parameters to schedule compute resources to process the additional one or more frames for the workload; and
updating the compute resource parameters in the local cache memory.

receiving an additional one or more frames for the workload;
retrieving the one or more compute resource parameters from the local cache memory; and
using the compute resource parameters to schedule compute resources to process the additional one or more frames for the workload.

receive, in a general purpose graphics processor comprising a plurality of streaming multiprocessors (SMs) comprising a plurality of processing resources and a local cache memory, one or more frames for a workload;
determine one or more compute resource parameters of the plurality of streaming microprocessors for the workload;
use the compute resource parameters to schedule compute resources to process the additional one or more frames for the workload; and
update the compute resource parameters in the local cache memory.

receive an additional one or more frames for the workload;
retrieve the one or more compute resource parameters from the local cache memory; and
use the compute resource parameters to schedule compute resources to process the additional one or more frames for the workload.
